WEBVTT

00:00:02.660 --> 00:00:05.640
Present Day

00:00:05.350 --> 00:00:08.590
Present Time

00:00:17.010 --> 00:00:23.340
And you don't seem to understand

00:00:22.090 --> 00:00:28.540
A shame you seemed an honest man

00:00:26.790 --> 00:00:33.290
And all the fears you hold so dear

00:00:31.920 --> 00:00:38.560
Will turn to whisper in your ear

00:00:37.390 --> 00:00:41.960
And you know what they say might hurt you

00:00:40.130 --> 00:00:44.430
And you know that it means so much

00:00:42.690 --> 00:00:49.190
And you don't even feel a thing

00:00:47.890 --> 00:00:54.850
I am falling, I am fading

00:00:53.040 --> 00:00:58.970
I have lost it all

00:01:17.720 --> 00:01:26.990
I am falling, I am fading, I am drowning

00:01:25.440 --> 00:01:29.630
Help me to breathe

00:01:27.660 --> 00:01:34.840
I am hurting, I have lost it all

00:01:33.200 --> 00:01:37.380
I am losing

00:01:35.770 --> 00:01:41.580
Help me to breathe

00:02:08.980 --> 00:02:12.190
I'll tell you, but it's just between you and me.

00:02:12.190 --> 00:02:16.190
I'll tell you what's happening in this society, what's beginning

00:02:16.190 --> 00:02:18.320
just because you don't know about it.

00:03:01.310 --> 00:03:03.700
No, that's not it.

00:03:04.550 --> 00:03:06.530
I'm just watching.

00:03:07.180 --> 00:03:09.930
I mean, the me in the Wired is...

00:03:11.220 --> 00:03:14.740
Right. She's becoming less and less like me.

00:03:17.330 --> 00:03:19.530
I don't really know.

00:03:20.200 --> 00:03:22.510
Huh? Who?

00:03:39.480 --> 00:03:41.360
Sis?

00:03:49.230 --> 00:03:52.440
My sister's been acting different lately.

00:03:53.900 --> 00:03:57.110
I... I'm not sure.

00:03:57.970 --> 00:03:58.790
Right.

00:04:00.370 --> 00:04:02.270
Fine, suit yourself.

00:04:04.960 --> 00:04:06.910
I know.

00:04:06.910 --> 00:04:11.470
The real world and the Wired are attached end to end.

00:04:13.950 --> 00:04:16.470
I can exist anywhere.

00:04:16.470 --> 00:04:21.330
No matter where my body is, I can send my consciousness anywhere I want.

00:04:54.860 --> 00:04:58.140
It's time for the EMA Motor Consortium banquet.

00:04:58.470 --> 00:04:59.910
Right.

00:05:08.340 --> 00:05:09.930
Mail.

00:05:09.930 --> 00:05:12.620
I'll be down in three minutes.

00:05:14.210 --> 00:05:16.040
Very well.

00:05:45.910 --> 00:05:48.530
What game do you want to play this time?

00:06:29.650 --> 00:06:31.260
Try some of this...

00:06:35.990 --> 00:06:38.120
That's right, you morons.

00:06:38.490 --> 00:06:41.410
I'm better than you bozos!

00:06:50.710 --> 00:06:54.590
The real world isn't real at all.

00:06:56.150 --> 00:06:57.460
Lain?

00:07:00.920 --> 00:07:02.400
Are you okay?

00:07:02.990 --> 00:07:03.940
Why do you ask?

00:07:04.270 --> 00:07:07.940
Lately, you've been... slipping again, Lain.

00:07:11.860 --> 00:07:18.410
We... We wanted to make you happy, so we've been taking you out with us.

00:07:22.410 --> 00:07:25.060
That's what we were trying to do. Honest.

00:07:25.060 --> 00:07:29.820
But if you weren't happy, I apologize.

00:07:31.350 --> 00:07:32.840
No! That's not it.

00:07:33.200 --> 00:07:36.430
Of course I was having fun.

00:07:38.190 --> 00:07:40.390
I've had a great time.

00:07:55.100 --> 00:07:56.690
Glad to hear it.

00:08:02.040 --> 00:08:03.470
Arisu!

00:08:03.470 --> 00:08:04.300
Yeah?

00:08:04.650 --> 00:08:09.830
Um... Thanks. Thanks for worrying about me.

00:08:11.350 --> 00:08:13.570
That's what friends are for, right?

00:08:13.570 --> 00:08:15.100
See you.

00:08:27.670 --> 00:08:32.630
This afternoon, the firewall of the Information Bureau's

00:08:32.630 --> 00:08:35.730
Information Control Center was cracked and destroyed by some party,

00:08:35.730 --> 00:08:40.130
and information in the Wired Network is currently in disarray.

00:08:40.480 --> 00:08:44.760
This news report is being sent out at this moment,

00:08:44.760 --> 00:08:51.420
but please be aware that it may arrive tomorrow, or possibly yesterday.

00:08:55.600 --> 00:08:57.300
Looks like it was the Knights.

00:08:57.300 --> 00:08:58.880
"Knights"? Who's that?

00:09:00.440 --> 00:09:03.030
"Knights." The Knights of the Eastern Calculus,

00:09:03.030 --> 00:09:05.550
said to have great influence in the Wired.

00:09:05.550 --> 00:09:08.890
Members comprising the group: Unknown.

00:09:08.890 --> 00:09:11.830
They are not only involved in mere information manipulation,

00:09:11.830 --> 00:09:14.300
they also are involved in the development and distribution

00:09:14.300 --> 00:09:16.740
of illegal information devices.

00:09:17.320 --> 00:09:19.360
I hear somebody's after Lain!

00:09:19.360 --> 00:09:20.200
Lain? Who's that?

00:09:20.620 --> 00:09:25.040
Lain. Search has no matches.

00:09:25.490 --> 00:09:27.580
I haven't seen Lain around lately.

00:09:27.580 --> 00:09:28.980
Who the hell is Lain?

00:09:28.980 --> 00:09:30.220
A girl.

00:09:30.220 --> 00:09:31.350
A girl?

00:09:31.350 --> 00:09:32.390
She's powerful!

00:09:32.390 --> 00:09:33.510
How?

00:09:34.570 --> 00:09:37.830
Her metamorphosis. Her will. Her power.

00:09:37.830 --> 00:09:39.690
The light in her eyes. Her existence.

00:09:43.550 --> 00:09:45.700
Hey, can I ask you something?

00:09:45.700 --> 00:09:46.260
What?

00:09:46.540 --> 00:09:49.450
You wouldn't happen to be a Knights member, would you?

00:10:00.460 --> 00:10:01.840
Just a minute!

00:10:03.700 --> 00:10:05.570
Delivery, ma'am!

00:10:06.140 --> 00:10:08.200
Let me get my stamp.

00:10:13.280 --> 00:10:16.230
I'm sorry, I didn't mean to keep you waiting so long.

00:10:16.230 --> 00:10:17.000
That's okay, ma'am.

00:10:18.150 --> 00:10:19.390
Okay, here's my stamp.

00:10:20.080 --> 00:10:21.000
What is it?

00:10:21.000 --> 00:10:22.470
That Navi.

00:10:22.470 --> 00:10:24.600
That's a new model, right? I wish I had one.

00:10:26.060 --> 00:10:28.470
I bought it with money from my home job.

00:10:28.470 --> 00:10:33.770
Even working at a job like this, I'd never be able to buy one of those.

00:10:33.770 --> 00:10:34.340
Here you are.

00:10:34.340 --> 00:10:35.770
Well, keep working for it.

00:10:37.320 --> 00:10:37.980
Sure thing.

00:10:38.430 --> 00:10:42.150
Yeah, you're right. If I don't work hard, I'll never...

00:10:42.570 --> 00:10:46.530
If you have trouble with anything, let me know. I can teach you.

00:10:49.710 --> 00:10:51.000
You'll teach me?

00:10:51.300 --> 00:10:54.000
Sure. I'm pretty good.

00:10:54.550 --> 00:10:58.310
So this is how you seduce bored housewives, huh?

00:10:58.310 --> 00:10:59.940
No, I just...

00:10:59.940 --> 00:11:01.440
Well, maybe a little.

00:11:01.440 --> 00:11:02.380
I'm home!

00:11:04.690 --> 00:11:06.410
Well, thanks.

00:11:13.640 --> 00:11:19.650
Mom, can I go over to Kinya's to play later?

00:11:20.080 --> 00:11:23.150
If you're going to play a game, can't you just do it over the Net?

00:11:23.810 --> 00:11:26.660
He's gonna teach me how to play it!

00:11:30.790 --> 00:11:34.030
The Wired and the real world are one and the same.

00:11:54.880 --> 00:11:56.830
W-What?

00:11:58.480 --> 00:12:03.560
Ms. Iwakura Lain. Would you please come with us?

00:12:05.320 --> 00:12:09.880
We won't force you. This is a request.

00:12:11.830 --> 00:12:16.940
We have no intention to harm you physically.

00:12:17.870 --> 00:12:19.350
Who are you?

00:12:27.140 --> 00:12:31.890
If you come with us, we'll tell you.

00:12:41.960 --> 00:12:47.340
I... I don't want to be here. You understand that, don't you?

00:12:47.760 --> 00:12:50.750
Just look at all I can do! Look!

00:12:51.200 --> 00:12:55.120
I'm breaking the barrier between the real world and the Wired.

00:12:57.740 --> 00:13:01.900
Come on, I think I'm plenty qualified.

00:13:01.900 --> 00:13:04.550
Let me into the Knights!

00:13:06.950 --> 00:13:08.760
You're impressed, huh?

00:13:09.150 --> 00:13:11.220
I tracked you down all by myself!

00:13:11.610 --> 00:13:14.480
This is your dedicated top-secret channel, right?

00:13:14.480 --> 00:13:17.470
Come on, make me one of you!

00:13:28.320 --> 00:13:30.040
W-Who are you?!

00:14:07.050 --> 00:14:11.970
Tachibana General Laboratories - Shinbashi Office

00:14:29.770 --> 00:14:32.220
Could you come here for a minute?

00:14:33.010 --> 00:14:36.750
I can't seem to get the main office's firewall to recognize this machine.

00:14:37.240 --> 00:14:40.020
I've done everything I can on the app end of things.

00:14:45.280 --> 00:14:50.030
I guess it's hopeless with an old machine like this.

00:14:50.990 --> 00:14:53.440
But I've always used this thing...

00:14:53.440 --> 00:14:57.270
I just can't work up the interest to switch over to a new Navi.

00:14:58.910 --> 00:15:01.040
Not at my age.

00:15:05.570 --> 00:15:08.040
If I were as young as you, though...

00:15:11.710 --> 00:15:13.690
That jumper there.

00:15:17.710 --> 00:15:21.500
Try removing this jumper and that one over there.

00:15:21.950 --> 00:15:24.690
Sorry, could you do it for me?

00:15:47.840 --> 00:15:49.520
Authorized.

00:15:54.520 --> 00:15:57.660
L-Lain? You're one of the Knights?!

00:15:58.820 --> 00:16:03.310
You are, aren't you, Lain? I had no idea!

00:16:05.930 --> 00:16:07.280
Moron.

00:16:07.980 --> 00:16:10.170
W-Wait! Please!

00:16:10.530 --> 00:16:14.090
That game you've been playing with those kids lately is the greatest!

00:16:14.090 --> 00:16:17.860
But I have an even better idea.

00:16:18.890 --> 00:16:23.290
So, please! Make me one of you! Make me a Knight!

00:16:23.970 --> 00:16:26.410
Please, make me one of you!

00:16:26.770 --> 00:16:31.800
Some say that the Wired doesn't have political borders like the real world.

00:16:32.510 --> 00:16:34.850
But there are far too many

00:16:35.260 --> 00:16:40.430
nonsense-spouting anarchists or idiots who think that pranks are a revolution.

00:16:40.430 --> 00:16:45.430
But the Knights don't seem to be either of those.

00:16:47.370 --> 00:16:48.440
Knights...

00:16:48.720 --> 00:16:53.360
I'm don't know how much of what you do is intentional.

00:16:53.360 --> 00:16:58.450
Your presence in the Wired is highly unnatural.

00:16:58.800 --> 00:17:04.450
And the Knights seem to have a special interest in you.

00:17:04.450 --> 00:17:09.460
I... I don't... I don't understand what you're...

00:17:09.740 --> 00:17:14.810
The Knights... You've been in direct contact with them at some point.

00:17:14.810 --> 00:17:17.920
But I... I don't...

00:17:18.470 --> 00:17:23.970
At any rate, it looks like they want to use you for something.

00:17:23.970 --> 00:17:29.480
We believe that is something that must be prevented, no matter the cost.

00:17:30.110 --> 00:17:34.480
W-What... are you? Who are you?

00:17:45.640 --> 00:17:48.870
Your secret's safe with me. You bet!

00:17:49.650 --> 00:17:54.180
You believe in Deus, right? I'll follow your lead.

00:17:54.180 --> 00:17:59.260
But is it true? Is God really in the Wired?

00:17:59.910 --> 00:18:02.360
I'm not ready to believe that yet.

00:18:02.360 --> 00:18:05.700
But if you let me join you, I'll be able to learn more.

00:18:05.700 --> 00:18:08.460
Then I'll believe!

00:18:12.520 --> 00:18:13.930
Is that you?

00:18:14.520 --> 00:18:16.160
You came!

00:18:16.590 --> 00:18:18.510
You came for me!

00:18:20.250 --> 00:18:21.410
My name...

00:18:22.460 --> 00:18:25.250
It's meaningless to know my real name.

00:18:25.720 --> 00:18:28.330
I, and those gentlemen there, have no name.

00:18:30.170 --> 00:18:31.950
Tell me.

00:18:33.140 --> 00:18:38.630
Iwakura Lain, are you and the Lain of the Wired one and the same?

00:18:41.070 --> 00:18:42.940
Who are you?

00:18:42.940 --> 00:18:45.700
I... I'm...

00:18:45.700 --> 00:18:48.770
Are your parents your real parents?

00:18:49.120 --> 00:18:50.300
Huh?

00:18:50.300 --> 00:18:52.640
Is your sister your real sister?

00:18:52.940 --> 00:18:57.150
W-What are you saying? O-Of course they are...

00:18:57.440 --> 00:19:00.150
When is your father's birthday?

00:19:01.270 --> 00:19:03.650
Dad's... His...

00:19:04.050 --> 00:19:09.030
What about your mother's birthday? When did your parents get married?

00:19:09.030 --> 00:19:10.660
Did they meet, or was it arranged?

00:19:10.660 --> 00:19:15.460
T-That's... I...

00:19:16.150 --> 00:19:19.670
Why don't you know? You never asked?

00:19:20.190 --> 00:19:24.410
You've never celebrated a birthday in your family? Not since you were little?

00:19:24.410 --> 00:19:25.470
Well?

00:19:29.680 --> 00:19:33.450
When were you born? Where?

00:19:36.000 --> 00:19:39.690
I... What does it matter? It...

00:19:40.010 --> 00:19:43.330
You don't know? You don't know anything?

00:19:45.610 --> 00:19:49.670
Are you okay? You don't know anything.

00:19:53.460 --> 00:19:54.830
Shut up, damn it...

00:19:55.590 --> 00:19:59.540
Who cares about that crap? Like any of it matters...

00:20:05.270 --> 00:20:07.720
You're Lain of the Wired?

00:20:08.640 --> 00:20:10.520
So what if I am?

00:20:12.110 --> 00:20:16.840
If you're here without a device, you know that the border between

00:20:16.840 --> 00:20:21.050
the real world and the Wired is starting to crumble, don't you?

00:20:21.050 --> 00:20:22.150
So?

00:20:22.150 --> 00:20:25.240
We believe that to be dangerous.

00:20:26.190 --> 00:20:27.930
Sounds interesting.

00:20:34.030 --> 00:20:35.040
Move it.

00:20:41.210 --> 00:20:42.860
What's the big idea?

00:20:42.860 --> 00:20:46.170
You are what's dangerous.

00:20:48.840 --> 00:20:50.390
Karl!

00:20:58.690 --> 00:21:03.370
It's as she said. Something interesting is beginning.

00:21:03.370 --> 00:21:06.440
We should just watch from the sidelines.

00:21:11.130 --> 00:21:12.620
Shou!

00:21:12.620 --> 00:21:14.120
Yeah, Mom?

00:21:14.640 --> 00:21:16.490
Let me play, too!

00:21:17.010 --> 00:21:18.790
Are you done with work?

00:21:18.790 --> 00:21:19.950
You bet!

00:21:19.950 --> 00:21:21.920
I'm the greatest!

00:21:22.380 --> 00:21:25.300
I'm gonna get ya, Shou!

00:21:26.150 --> 00:21:28.300
See? Say your prayers!

00:21:29.850 --> 00:21:31.170
Watch this!

00:22:29.490 --> 00:22:33.920
nan no tsumi mo nai hazu na no ni

00:22:29.490 --> 00:22:33.920
Although I must be innocent,

00:22:33.920 --> 00:22:37.830
nanraka no batsu wo uketeru

00:22:33.920 --> 00:22:37.830
now I am punished.

00:22:38.260 --> 00:22:44.130
jibun de maita tane de mo nai no ni

00:22:38.260 --> 00:22:44.130
I wasn't the one who sowed those seeds, but nevertheless

00:22:44.850 --> 00:22:51.040
sakimidareta hana tsumasareru

00:22:44.850 --> 00:22:51.040
I have to pull up the flowers that bloomed from them.

00:22:57.590 --> 00:23:02.230
shiranai koto to mo ienai ga

00:22:57.590 --> 00:23:02.230
I can't say I didn't know about it,

00:23:02.230 --> 00:23:06.680
katabou katsuida oboe wa nai

00:23:02.230 --> 00:23:06.680
but I don't remember taking any part in it.

00:23:06.680 --> 00:23:12.870
jiyuu wo takaku kawasareta ki mo suru ga

00:23:06.680 --> 00:23:12.870
I think my freedom cost me dearly,

00:23:13.400 --> 00:23:20.110
kokoro made yasuku utta oboe wa nai

00:23:13.400 --> 00:23:20.110
but I don't remember selling my soul so cheaply.

00:23:20.470 --> 00:23:28.160
Hey Hey kutabatte osaraba suru made

00:23:20.470 --> 00:23:28.160
Hey hey, until I die and say farewell...

00:23:29.180 --> 00:23:38.070
Hey Hey dare no te ni mo kakaranai

00:23:29.180 --> 00:23:38.070
Hey hey... no one can touch me.

00:23:39.590 --> 00:23:43.680
tooi yoru wo urotsuiteiru

00:23:39.590 --> 00:23:43.680
You probably don't know

00:23:43.680 --> 00:23:51.390
shiranai darou eien no narazu monotachi wo

00:23:43.680 --> 00:23:51.390
the eternal outlaws prowling in the distant night.
